{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.gate_not_a_function_of_displayed_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.gate_not_a_function_of_displayed_data","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L215-L235","doc":"**The producer's gate is not a function of the data the block's formula\ndisplays.**\n\nTwo trace vectors that agree on *every* value the displayed formula reads —\n`f (τ i)` for all `i` — give different gated totals.  So there is no way to\nwrite the producer's functional in the block's own variables: the gate needs the\nsign, and `ln|tr|` has already thrown it away.\n\nThis is the resolution's load-bearing theorem.  It says the mismatch is\nstructural, not editorial: the block's text is not a loose paraphrase of the\nproducer, it is a formula that *cannot* denote what the producer computes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.resolventScale_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.resolventScale_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L192-L204","doc":"**The resolvent factor never supplies a sign.**\n\nNon-negative whenever its four inputs are, so adding it to the content block\nchanges the magnitude of every per-partition term and the sign of none.  This is\nwhy divergence 2 is a statable omission rather than a disagreement: the block's\nformula is the producer's with one non-negative factor deleted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.resolventScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.resolventScale","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L184-L190","doc":"The resolvent-damped scale `m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · ρ_λ(s)` with\n`ρ_λ(s) = 1/(μ_λ + s)` — the factor the producer applies\n(`hecke_core_legacy.py:548`, `:1915`) and the content block omits.  `def:q-resolvent`\ngives `R_q(s) = (s + Δ̂_q)⁻¹`; on the `λ`-block of the Wedderburn decomposition\nthat is the scalar `1/(μ_λ + s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L163-L176","doc":"**A non-negative scale against a non-positive log-ratio forces `B ≤ 0`.**\n\nThe Lean form of `computations/probes/uic_sign_forced_by_gate_probe.py`: the\nper-partition scale `m_e · H_q · y_λ · ρ_λ` is non-negative factor by factor\n(measured: negative in 0 of 682 partitions), so the sign of the gated total is\ndecided entirely by the sign of the log-ratios on the selected set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.cs_selection_excludes_log_domain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.cs_selection_excludes_log_domain","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L145-L155","doc":"**The genuine complementary-slackness set meets the log summand's domain\nnowhere.**\n\n`ln|x|` is the honest logarithm only where `x ≠ 0`; complementary slackness\nselects exactly `x = 0`.  Stated over sets, so no decidability is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_cs_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_cs_eq","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L126-L142","doc":"**Genuine complementary slackness collapses the functional to a constant.**\n\nFor a Frobenius positivity constraint `⟨Φ, π_λ⟩ ≥ 0`, complementary slackness\nmakes \"tight\" mean `tr = 0` — not `tr ≤ 0`, which is what the producer codes.\nUnder the genuine condition every selected block contributes the *same* value\n`f 0`, so the total is `(Σ_{selected} c_λ) · f 0`: it reads nothing about the\natom.  A selection rule that cannot vary with the nucleus cannot be the source\nof a nucleus-dependent binding energy, so complementary slackness does not\njustify the coded gate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_eq_uicAll_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_eq_uicAll_iff","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L115-L124","doc":"**The two functionals agree iff the excluded blocks contribute nothing.**\n\nSo \"gate or no gate\" is not a matter of degree that a tolerance could absorb:\nthey coincide on exactly the measure-zero condition that the slack blocks cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_add_compl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated_add_compl","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**The gated and ungated totals differ by exactly the excluded blocks.**\n\nImmediate, but it is the statement that makes the 3.4-4.6× measured gap a\n*quantity* rather than a discrepancy: it is the sum over the slack blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicAll_sign_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicAll_sign_blind","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L87-L102","doc":"**The block's functional is blind to the sign of the trace.**\n\nIts summand reads the trace only through `|tr|` (evenness hypothesis `hf`), so\nflipping the sign of any subset of the block traces leaves the total unchanged.\nThis is exactly the invariance the displayed formula `ln|tr M_λ| − ln d_λ`\nmanifestly has. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicGated","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L80-L85","doc":"The UIC accumulator summed over a **selected** set of blocks, as\n`hecke_core_legacy.unified_iterative_correction` Pass 2 computes it.  The\nproducer's selector is `sel i := (τ i ≤ 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicAll","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection.uicAll","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICFunctionalSelection.lean#L69-L78","doc":"The UIC accumulator summed over **every** block, as\n`prop:unified-iterative-correction` states it.\n\n`c i` is the per-partition scale `m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · ρ_λ(s_*)`, `τ i` is the\n**signed** final Markov trace of block `i`, and `f` is the displayed summand\n`x ↦ ln|x| − ln d`.  Writing it this way keeps the two arguments the block's\nformula actually reads — the scale and the summand — separate from the sign,\nwhich is what the theorems below turn on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}